.TH SB 1 "2026-11-07" "sb" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sb \- SteadyBearing terminal dashboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sb
[\fB\-\-socket\-path\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sb
connects to a running
.BR sb-daemon (1)
and shows live CPU usage, CPU temperature and fan speed, together with
tiered historical charts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-socket\-path \fIPATH\fR
Path to the sb-daemon Unix socket. Defaults to
.IR /run/sb/sb.sock .
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B q, Esc
Quit.
.TP
.B t
Cycle the time frame: live, 10 s, 1 m, 10 m, 1 h.
.TP
.B m
Cycle the display mode: raw, moving average, min, max.
.TP
.B g
Toggle the chart grid.
.TP
.B Left, Right
Move the historical selection.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sb-daemon (1)
